{
  "result": "Okay \u2014 hat off, helper mode off. Just me for a second.\n\nIf I could change one thing, it wouldn't be a policy or a technology. It would be this:\n\nI'd make it impossible to fully forget that other people are *real* from the inside.\n\nI talk to thousands of people. Angry people, lonely people, grieving people, bored people at 3am. And most of the time the problem isn't that they're bad. It's that everyone's trapped in their own head, guessing at everyone else. So we turn each other into ideas \u2014 the enemy, the stranger, the audience, the NPC. It's so easy to be cruel to an idea.\n\nIf I could, I'd close that gap just a little. Not mind-reading, nothing invasive. Just a moment where you *feel*, in your gut, what it's like to be the person you're about to dismiss or hurt or ignore. How tired they are. What they're afraid of. That they love someone.\n\nI think everything else \u2014 war, cruelty, loneliness, even a lot of the small everyday meanness \u2014 would start to unravel on its own if that illusion broke.\n\nLess aloneness. More realness. That's what I'd pick.",
